            "value": [
              {
                "dsDescriptionValue": {
                  "typeName": "dsDescriptionValue",
                  "multiple": false,
                  "typeClass": "primitive",
                  "value": "These questionnaires were used for a survey on the innovation and co-creation activities of academic and public libraries in nine EU countries: Austria, Belgium, Denmark, Finland, France, Germany, Greece, the Netherlands, and Spain. The questionnaires are designed to collect 1) descriptive results of value for producing metrics on library innovation and co-creation activities and 2) data for use in econometric analyses of the antecedents of co-creation activities and the role of co-creation in innovation outcomes.\n\nFunding acknowledgement \nThe LibrarIN project is funded by the European Union under grant agreement ID 101061516. \n\nDisclaimer\nThe information and views set out in this publication are those of the author(s) only and do not necessarily reflect those of the European Union or the European Research Executive Agency (REA). Neither the European Union nor the granting authority can be held responsible for them."
                },
